---
title: Stuart rotates a key with a CAS Beacon, Satoshi verifies
---

%% Use case: Stuart and Satoshi are peers in a p2p, Signal-like messaging channel.
%% Each peer is identified by a did:btcr2 DID. Satoshi trusts Stuart's keys at version N.
%% The aggregation steps follow the RECOMMENDED MuSig2 example of the specification.

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Stu as Stuart (Aggregation Participant)
    participant Others as Other Aggregation Participants
    participant AS as Aggregation Service
    participant BTC as Bitcoin blockchain ⛓
    participant CAS as CAS / IPFS 📦 (optional)
    actor Sat as Satoshi (channel peer)
    participant Res as Satoshi's resolver

    rect rgba(128, 128, 128, 0.08)
    Note over Stu,AS: 0. Setup, one time: join a CAS Aggregation Cohort
    Stu->>AS: Enroll: did, Schnorr public key
    AS->>Stu: n-of-n P2TR Beacon Address and the n public keys
    Stu->>Stu: Compute the address again. Make sure that it contains Stuart's key.
    Stu->>BTC: Update the DID to add a CASBeacon service<br/>(announced through the Singleton Beacon)
    end

    rect rgba(128, 128, 128, 0.08)
    Note over Stu: 1. Construct the update
    Stu->>Stu: Resolve own DID (minConf 6) → versionId N
    Stu->>Stu: Construct and sign the BTCR2 Update with the new key material<br/>(targetVersionId N + 1), then verify the proof
    Stu->>Stu: updateHash = SHA256(JCS(BTCR2 Signed Update))
    end

    rect rgba(128, 128, 128, 0.08)
    Note over Stu,BTC: 2. Aggregate and announce (the cohort sees which DIDs have an update)
    AS->>Stu: Update opportunity
    AS->>Others: Update opportunity
    par Every participant responds
        Stu->>AS: did, updateHash, MuSig2 nonce
    and
        Others->>AS: did and updateHash, or no update, MuSig2 nonce
    end
    AS->>AS: Build the CAS Announcement { did: updateHash }.<br/>Signal Bytes = SHA256(JCS(CAS Announcement)). Aggregate the nonces.
    AS->>Stu: CAS Announcement, Unsigned Beacon Signal, aggregated nonce
    AS->>Others: CAS Announcement, Unsigned Beacon Signal, aggregated nonce
    Stu->>Stu: Check: the entry for Stuart's DID = updateHash,<br/>no entry for a DID of Stuart without an update,<br/>Signal Bytes = hash of the CAS Announcement
    Stu->>AS: Partial signature
    Others->>AS: Partial signatures
    AS->>BTC: Aggregate the partial signatures, broadcast the Beacon Signal
    BTC-->>Stu: minConf (6) confirmations
    Stu->>Stu: Keep the update and the CAS Announcement for the life of the DID
    Note over Stu,AS: In each later round, Stuart responds with no update.<br/>Stuart keeps the CAS Announcement of each Beacon Signal.
    end

    rect rgba(128, 128, 128, 0.08)
    Note over Stu,Sat: 3. Distribute the update data
    alt CAS distribution (public)
        Stu->>CAS: Publish the CAS Announcement and the BTCR2 Signed Update
    else Sidecar distribution (private)
        Stu->>Stu: Keep the data for the Sidecar Data
    end
    Stu->>Sat: Channel message signed with the new key, did, and Sidecar Data:<br/>updates, casUpdates (if Sidecar distribution)
    end

    rect rgba(128, 128, 128, 0.08)
    Note over Sat,Res: 4. Satoshi verifies
    Sat->>Res: resolve(did, { sidecar })
    Res->>BTC: Find Beacon Signals of the Singleton and CAS Beacon Addresses
    BTC-->>Res: Beacon Signals (Signal Bytes = hash of a CAS Announcement), block metadata
    alt CAS Announcement in the Sidecar Data
        Res->>Res: Get it from cas_lookup_table
    else not in the Sidecar Data
        Res->>CAS: Get the CAS Announcement by the Signal Bytes
    end
    alt Entry for Stuart's DID
        Res->>Res: Get the update by the entry value (Sidecar Data, else CAS)
        Res->>Res: Process Next Update: check the hashes and the proof, apply the patch
    else no entry
        Res->>Res: No update for Stuart's DID in this Beacon Signal
    end
    Res-->>Sat: didDocument (version N + 1) and didDocumentMetadata
    Sat->>Sat: Check: not deactivated, versionId ≥ N, new key is in authentication.<br/>Verify the channel message with the new key. Trust the new key.
    end
